{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":807,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.70","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 70","reference":"Psalms 70","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"This psalm is copied almost word for word from the eleventh psalm, and perhaps is for that reason entitled, A psalm to bring remembrance."},{"verse":2,"text":"For it may sometimes be of use to pray over again the prayers we have formerly made to God on like occasions."},{"verse":3,"text":"David here prays, that God would send help to him, shame to his enemies, and joy to his friends."},{"verse":4,"text":"To the chief musician, a psalm of David, to bring to remembrance."}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":70}}